                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  I_{g,n,\beta} :
                  H^*(X)^{\otimes}
                  \\to
                  H^*(\bar M_{g,n}(X,\beta))
                  \\stackrel{\phi_*}{\to}
                  H^*(\bar M_{g,n})
          %p
            where the map
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi ϕ
                    %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi_*
            is some kind of “pushforward” or “integration along the fibers”; this map uses the virtual fundamental class
          %p there is also a map
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi α
                  %mo :
